/* qBittorrent Native — Windows Dark */
QToolBar#toolBar {
    background: #202020;
    color: #F5F5F5;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #323232;
    spacing: 0px;
    padding: 0px 6px;
    margin: 0px;
    min-height: 42px;
    max-height: 42px;
    qproperty-iconSize: 22px 22px;
}
/*
   No QToolButton min-height/max-height (or hover/pressed background) rule
   here on purpose: on non-integer display scaling, styling QToolButton
   inside this toolbar was found (on macOS, confirmed by direct A/B testing)
   to misplace the leading search-icon of the neighboring "Filter torrents"
   QLineEdit, even though the two are different widgets. Applying the same
   defensive omission here since the same toolbar layout is shared across
   all variants. Buttons render with default/native look until a
   narrower-scoped fix is found.
*/
QToolBar#toolBar QLabel { color: #F5F5F5; background: transparent; }
QToolBar#toolBar QLineEdit,
QToolBar#toolBar QComboBox {
    color: #F5F5F5;
    background: #2B2B2B;
    border: 1px solid #454545;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 3px 7px;
    selection-background-color: #005FB8;
}
QToolBar#toolBar QComboBox { padding-right: 22px; }
QToolBar#toolBar QComboBox::drop-down { border: none; width: 20px; }
QToolBar#toolBar QComboBox QAbstractItemView {
    color: #F5F5F5;
    background: #2B2B2B;
    selection-background-color: #005FB8;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}
QToolBar#toolBar QToolButton::menu-indicator {
    image: url(:/uitheme/icons/chevron-down.svg);
    width: 10px;
    height: 7px;
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: center right;
    right: 1px;
}
/*
   qBittorrent 5.2.3 on macOS converts toolbar separators into ordinary
   QWidget spacers with minimumWidth=16. It also adds two 8px QWidget
   spacers. Because they are no longer QToolBar::separator objects, styling
   QToolBar::separator alone cannot remove them on macOS. Included here too
   (not just in the macOS variants) since this platform-branded theme file
   can still end up loaded by a macOS build of qBittorrent.

   Match those exact spacer widgets by their minimumWidth Qt property and
   reset the QWidget geometry properties themselves. The expanding spacer
   that pushes Search/Filter to the right has no 8/16px minimumWidth and is
   intentionally left untouched.
*/
QToolBar#toolBar QWidget[minimumWidth="16"],
QToolBar#toolBar QWidget[minimumWidth="8"] {
    qproperty-minimumWidth: 0;
    qproperty-maximumWidth: 0;
    min-width: 0px;
    max-width: 0px;
    width: 0px;
    margin: 0px;
    padding: 0px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
}

QToolBar#toolBar::separator,
QToolBar::separator { width: 0px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: none; background: transparent; }

QListWidget#categoriesList,
QListView#categoriesList { background: transparent; border: none; outline: none; }
QListWidget#categoriesList::item,
QListView#categoriesList::item {
    color: #F5F5F5;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: 4px 6px;
    margin: 1px 2px;
    border-radius: 4px;
}
QListWidget#categoriesList::item:hover,
QListView#categoriesList::item:hover { background: #2D2D2D; }
QListWidget#categoriesList::item:selected,
QListView#categoriesList::item:selected { background: #005FB8; color: #FFFFFF; }
